"agentic_understanding":"Anchored on identity_resolution_snapshot (Homo sapiens; EC 1.1.1.39; lead PMID 8593532) and confirmed no preserved accession candidate pool. Reviewed supporting PMIDs; evidence consistently describes a mitochondrial NAD(P)+-dependent malic enzyme that reacts with NAD+ and NADP+. Mapped the NAD(P)+-dependent mitochondrial activity to UniProtKB:P23368 (ME2) and populated the UniProt sequence as the resolved identity.","audit_history":["Loop 1: Extracted organism/substrate/PMID context and confirmed sequence unresolved in batch payload.","Loop 2: Retrieved and compared supporting PubMed abstracts for cofactor and compartment clues.","Loop 3: Selected UniProtKB:P23368 (ME2) as the accession-backed sequence matching the paper context and finalized verdict."],"critique_rationale":"Human malic enzyme isoforms include cytosolic NADP-dependent ME1 and mitochondrial NADP-dependent ME3 (strictly NADP+), but the batch evidence repeatedly describes an NAD(P)+-dependent enzyme active with NAD+ as well as NADP+. That cofactor profile and mitochondrial context supports ME2 over ME1/ME3.","review_loop_count":3,"review_summary":"Resolved the Homo sapiens NAD(P)+-dependent malic enzyme sequence to mitochondrial ME2 (UniProtKB:P23368) using the supporting PMID evidence.","sequence":"","sequence_source":"uniprotkb:P23368","smiles":null,"wild_type":false,"measurement_key":"6abbb4de25cee3e2","verification_method":"selected_batch_payload_review","cofactor_name":"NADP+","paper_grounding_status":"review_excerpt_preserved","paper_grounding_source":"review_notes_excerpt","paper_grounding_note":"Verification notes preserve a cited paper excerpt from manual review.","abstract_identity_anchor_state":null,"abstract_identity_anchor_note":null,"abstract_identity_anchor_hits":[],"paper_structure_signals":[],"paper_structure_note":null,"retrieval_trace_raw":null,"retrieval_source_type":null,"retrieval_selector":null,"retrieval_evidence_strength":null,"evidence_confidence_tier"